4	 * Implements the corpus filesystem over the Origin Private File System
5	 * (`navigator.storage.getDirectory()`). This is the always-on local working
6	 * copy; FSA mirror (S2) and git (S3) layer on top.
7	 *
8	 * Two contracts this file is responsible for (test-strategy G7/G8, arch-review):
9	 *  - SSR / unavailable guard: any call in an environment without
10	 *    `navigator.storage.getDirectory` rejects with a typed `CorpusError`
11	 *    ({kind:"unavailable"}), never a raw `TypeError`.
12	 *  - Failure reification: a quota failure rejects with {kind:"quota-exceeded",
13	 *    substrate:"opfs"} — it is NOT swallowed with console.warn the way the
14	 *    legacy localStorage adapter does (workspaceStore.ts:44-46).
15	 *
16	 * OPFS handle types are declared locally rather than relying on lib.dom, whose
17	 * OPFS surface (notably async `keys()`) varies by TypeScript version — keeping
18	 * our own minimal shapes makes the build stable across upgrades.
19	 */
